"## Flow: 9808\n\n- **Platform**: web\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/flows/9808\n- **Name**: Add audio comment to video timestamp\n- **Screens Count**: 7\n- **Description**: Happy path: A reviewer watches a video and adds an audio comment tied to the video's current timestamp. Entry point: reviewer has a video open with the comments panel visible and the timeline displayed (playhead at a specific time). Exit point: an audio comment (with playback UI and transcription/notes) appears in the comment thread, associated with the video's timestamp. Assumptions: the user can add comments (has commenting permissions), the browser has access to a microphone, and the player shows an active playhead/time (visible at 12:00 in screenshots).\n- **Problem**: Task the user is trying to accomplish: Attach an audio voice note to a specific point in the video so collaborators can hear contextual feedback. From the user's perspective: they expect to select a recording input/mode, record a short voice note while the video is at the desired timestamp, see a visual recording indicator and timer, and then have the audio appear in the conversation thread with playback controls and any processing/transcription states. From the interface/system perspective: the UI exposes a record action in the comment composer, a device/mode selector, a recording state (with timer and stop), and an upload/processing state. The system ties the resulting audio comment to the video's playhead time, stores/uploads the audio, and surfaces a player and snippet (and possibly a transcription) inside the comments list. User-perceived outcome: an audible comment appears inline in the conversation at the chosen timestamp with a visible waveform/player and any text notes. System-level outcome: an audio file is recorded, uploaded, processed (compiling insights/transcription), saved and associated with the video/timestamp.\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 821\n- **Name**: Flask.do\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/821\n- **Domain**: flask.do\n- **Categories**: Collaboration Tools\n- **Description**: Video collaboration platform \n\n### Steps\n\n#### Step 1: Video with comments visible\n- **Screen ID**: 1f541513-a976-470c-b507-56504bcedc1f\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/1f541513-a976-470c-b507-56504bcedc1f\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/3522c271-50a8-4724-b2c1-48a59621d83d_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Start review with the video and comment thread visible; identify the timestamp to annotate\n- **Action**: User observes the video player (playhead at 12:00) and the right-side comment panel; they decide to add a new comment at the current time\n- **System Response**: Player continues showing controls and timeline with markers; comment input area and a red circular record button are visible in the comment composer\n- **UX Patterns**: Comments, Video Player\n- **UI Elements**: Dropdown, Switch & Toggle, Text Field, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon, Avatar\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark-themed live concert video player with a social chat sidebar, featuring a main video, timeline scrubber, related video thumbnails, and message input controls.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout: a larger left video/control area with thumbnails and timeline, and a narrower right scrollable chat panel with a fixed message input at the bottom.\n  - Functions: Lets users watch and control the concert video, browse related clips, track playback progress, and read/send chat messages or voice comments while viewing.\n\n#### Step 2: Open recording/device options\n- **Screen ID**: 4120ed34-759e-4100-b6fe-bb086af1eebd\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/4120ed34-759e-4100-b6fe-bb086af1eebd\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/6895951a-ee09-4f22-8683-73b434bd54af_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Choose recording mode and input device before recording\n- **Action**: User clicks the red record button in the comment composer\n- **System Response**: A contextual device/mode selector appears above the composer (shows microphone and camera devices and a central REC MODE dial with options for Screen / Camera / Voice)\n- **UX Patterns**: Audio & Video Recorder\n- **UI Elements**: Tooltip\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark-mode multimedia interface with a central concert video player, a horizontal strip of preview thumbnails, a right-side live chat panel, and recording controls with device selectors and a red record button.\n  - Layout: Large main video area centered, timeline and thumbnail carousel below it, and a right column for chat plus stacked recording-mode controls near the bottom-right.\n  - Functions: Supports video playback controls, scrubbing, speed and volume adjustment, switching via preview thumbnails, chat viewing, and recording mode/device selection with start/stop recording.\n\n#### Step 3: Select voice recording mode\n- **Screen ID**: 64105fd8-6590-4a2c-bb05-9e862d6a4b85\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/64105fd8-6590-4a2c-bb05-9e862d6a4b85\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/b90913a1-990a-4510-9e6c-6026142e5f96_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Switch the recorder to voice-only mode and confirm input device\n- **Action**: User selects the Voice option on the REC MODE dial (and can choose the microphone from the device list)\n- **System Response**: UI highlights the Voice option and shows a tooltip indicating 'Record Voice' (also displaying a shortcut hint 'R' in the screenshot)\n- **UX Patterns**: Audio & Video Recorder\n- **UI Elements**: Tooltip\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark-themed concert video player with a large central playback window, related clip thumbnails, a progress timeline, and a right-side chat and recording control panel.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with the main video and controls centered/left, a thumbnail strip and timeline beneath, and a vertical right sidebar for chat and voice/camera controls.\n  - Functions: Lets users watch concert videos, browse related clips, scrub through playback, change speed, chat in real time, and switch or record using camera/microphone controls.\n\n#### Step 4: Start recording\n- **Screen ID**: c96a50fc-6ec5-48da-8e39-1015500c934f\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/c96a50fc-6ec5-48da-8e39-1015500c934f\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/4caf20ab-2a50-4cb2-96a8-4bd55d872e2a_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Begin capturing the audio comment tied to the current playhead time\n- **Action**: User presses the record control to start capturing audio\n- **System Response**: Composer switches to an active recording state — a small recording panel appears with a red timer (00:01) and an option to stop; the video and timeline remain visible so the comment aligns with the current timestamp\n- **UX Patterns**: Audio & Video Recorder\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Popover\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark-themed live concert video player with a band performance, timeline controls, thumbnail strip for more videos, and a right-side comments/audio panel.\n  - Layout: Wide main video area on the left with a bottom playback bar and overlaid video thumbnails; right sidebar holds chat comments and audio recording controls beneath a top header.\n  - Functions: Play and seek through concert videos, adjust playback speed, browse related thumbnails, read comments, share the session, and record or play audio messages in the sidebar.\n\n#### Step 5: Upload / processing state\n- **Screen ID**: 2776d1f0-369e-453e-98e2-ffa4c62dedff\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/2776d1f0-369e-453e-98e2-ffa4c62dedff\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/a747f085-7509-4116-aed5-1926e0f18160_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Let the system finish saving and processing the recorded audio\n- **Action**: After stopping, the user waits while the UI uploads and processes the audio\n- **System Response**: The composer shows progress and a status label ('Compiling insights...' and an uploading indicator). A waveform preview and a transient processing state are visible in the composer area\n- **UX Patterns**: Comments, Video Player\n- **UI Elements**: Dropdown, Switch & Toggle, Text Field, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon, Avatar\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark-mode concert video player with a live chat panel, showing playback controls, a thumbnail video carousel, timeline markers, and message input for commenting.\n  - Layout: Two-column desktop layout: large video/player area on the left and a scrollable chat/comments panel on the right, both on a black background.\n  - Functions: Supports video playback controls, timeline scrubbing, browsing related clips, and sending text or voice chat messages in a live discussion panel.\n\n#### Step 6: Add optional text/note to audio\n- **Screen ID**: 7f486ddd-bfd9-4cc8-9b8e-0166580c02f9\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/7f486ddd-bfd9-4cc8-9b8e-0166580c02f9\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/3805be59-b14a-4c93-a774-3bde3ef007eb_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Attach a short textual note or caption to the audio comment\n- **Action**: User types or pastes a short note into the comment input while the audio is attached (e.g., guidance text about what to find in the video)\n- **System Response**: Typed text appears above or alongside the audio attachment; the audio preview shows a timestamp (e.g., 0:15) and a waveform icon confirming the attachment\n- **UX Patterns**: Comments, Video Player\n- **UI Elements**: Dropdown, Switch & Toggle, Text Field, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon, Avatar\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark-themed concert video player with live chat, timeline markers, and thumbnail navigation.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a wide video player and timeline on the left, and a narrower chat panel with input controls on the right.\n  - Functions: Play and scrub concert video, jump via thumbnails or markers, adjust speed, and send/read live chat messages with optional voice input.\n\n#### Step 7: Audio comment appears in thread\n- **Screen ID**: a4720810-3058-4be7-b609-9f2acb38248d\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/a4720810-3058-4be7-b609-9f2acb38248d\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/flask.do/desktop/e69a314b-22bd-4852-98e6-c09670bec77e_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Confirm the audio comment is posted and playable in the conversation at the correct timestamp\n- **Action**: User views the comment thread where the new audio comment (with playback control, waveform and optional text) is displayed\n- **System Response**: The comment list updates with the new audio item showing its timestamp, play button, waveform preview and any user text; other comments remain visible and the video timeline still shows the playhead/markers\n- **UX Patterns**: Comments, Video Player\n- **UI Elements**: Dropdown, Switch & Toggle, Text Field, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon, Avatar\n- **Fonts**: UI Sans Serif, UI Monospace\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Dark modern video player for a concert with a large central playback area, thumbnail previews, a gradient timeline, and a right-side comments/notes feed.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout: a wide left media column with video, thumbnails, and controls; a narrow right sidebar for scrollable comments and an input area, topped by a simple header bar.\n  - Functions: Play and scrub the concert video, jump via thumbnails, adjust speed, review timestamped audio/text comments, add new notes, and share the page.\n\n### Related Queries\n- video review record voice\n- annotate timeline with audio\n- add audio comment timeline\n- in-context voice note recording\n- media review microphone selector\n- record comment attached time\n- comment thread audio upload\n- voice annotation playback controls\n- recording mode camera voice screen\n- audio comment processing indicator"
